<article class="env-lemma" id="0C1D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C1D">Lemma <span data-tag="0C1D">53.12.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of smooth proper curves over a field $k$ which satisfies the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/0C1C" data-tag="0C1C">53.12.1</a>. If $k = H^0(Y, \mathcal{O}_ Y) = H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $X$ and $Y$ have genus $g_ X$ and $g_ Y$, then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  2g_ X - 2 = (2g_ Y - 2) \deg (f) + \deg (R)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $R \subset X$ is the effective Cartier divisor cut out by the different of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See discussion above; we used Discriminants, Lemma <a href="/tag/0BWJ" data-tag="0BWJ">49.12.6</a>, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C1A" data-tag="0C1A">53.8.4</a>, and Varieties, Lemmas <a href="/tag/0AYX" data-tag="0AYX">33.44.7</a> and <a href="/tag/0AYZ" data-tag="0AYZ">33.44.11</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>